  "number": "10.1",
  "title": "Units of Measurement",
  "body": " Units of Measurement   Learning Outcomes   — Units and measurement  — Scale diagrams    The metric system uses base units: metres (length), kilograms (mass), litres (capacity), seconds (time). Prefixes indicate powers of ten: kilo- (×1000), centi- (×0.01), milli- (×0.001).  Common conversions:   1 km = 1000 m = 100 000 cm  1 kg = 1000 g  1 litre = 1000 ml  1 hour = 60 minutes = 3600 seconds   A scale diagram uses a ratio to represent a real object. If the scale is 1:50, then 1 cm on the diagram = 50 cm in reality.   Exercises   Convert 4.5 km to metres.  4500 m    A map has scale 1:20000. A road measures 6 cm on the map. How long is the actual road in kilometres?  1.2 km  Actual length = cm m km.    "
