  "title": "Triangle Properties",
  "body": " Triangle Properties   Learning Outcomes   — Angle sum in triangles and quadrilaterals  — Parallel lines and transversals  — Isosceles and equilateral triangles    The angles in any triangle add up to 180°. The angles in any quadrilateral add up to 360°.  An isosceles triangle has two equal sides and two equal base angles. An equilateral triangle has three equal sides and three 60° angles.  When a transversal crosses two parallel lines:   Alternate angles are equal (Z-angles)  Corresponding angles are equal (F-angles)  Co-interior angles are supplementary (add to 180°, C-angles)    Exercises   A triangle has angles and . Find the third angle.      An isosceles triangle has one angle of at the apex. Find the base angles.  Each base angle is .  The two base angles are equal. . Each base angle: .    "
