  "body": " Slope of a Line   Learning Outcomes   — Slope of a line  — Slope as rate of change    The slope (or gradient) of a line measures its steepness:   Positive slope: line goes up left-to-right. Negative slope: line goes down left-to-right. Zero slope: horizontal line. Undefined slope: vertical line.  Two lines are parallel if they have equal slopes: . Two lines are perpendicular if their slopes multiply to : .   Exercises   Find the slope of the line through and .      A line has slope . What is the slope of a perpendicular line?   Perpendicular slope:    "
