  "number": "14.1",
  "title": "Trigonometric Ratios",
  "body": " Trigonometric Ratios   Learning Outcomes   — Trigonometric ratios    In a right-angled triangle, label the sides relative to angle : the opposite side faces , the adjacent side is next to , and the hypotenuse is always opposite the right angle.  The three trigonometric ratios (remember SOH-CAH-TOA):   To find a missing side: identify which ratio links the known side and the unknown, then solve. To find a missing angle: use the inverse ratio, e.g. .   Exercises   In a right-angled triangle, the hypotenuse is 10 cm and one angle is 35°. Find the side opposite the 35° angle. Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.  5.74 cm  , so cm.    In a right-angled triangle, the opposite side is 6 cm and the adjacent side is 8 cm. Find the angle correct to 1 decimal place.  36.9°  , so .    "
