  "title": "Translations, Reflections, Rotations, and Enlargements",
  "body": " Translations, Reflections, Rotations, and Enlargements   Learning Outcomes   — Transformations  — Axes of symmetry  — Enlargements  — Enlargement and area    A translation slides every point by the same vector .  A reflection flips a shape across a mirror line (axis of symmetry). Every point and its image are the same distance from the mirror line.  A rotation turns a shape through an angle about a fixed centre point.  An enlargement with scale factor and centre maps every point to a point such that . Areas scale by : if a shape has area , its image has area .   Exercises   A triangle has area 12 cm². It is enlarged with scale factor 3. Find the area of the image.  108 cm²  Area scales by . New area: cm².    How many axes of symmetry does a regular hexagon have?  6    "
