  "body": " Graphing Functions   Learning Outcomes   — Graph linear functions  — Slope and intercept  — Graph quadratic functions (HL)  — Interpret graphs  — Graphs and stories  — Quantity and rate of change    A linear function has the form . The slope  gives the rate of change (steepness). The -intercept  is where the line crosses the -axis.  To graph a linear function, make a table of values, plot the points, and draw the line.  A quadratic function (HL) has the form and graphs as a parabola . The lowest (or highest) point is the vertex . The parabola is symmetric about the axis of symmetry .   Exercises   For , complete a table of values for , and state the slope and -intercept.  Slope: 2. -intercept: . Values: .    A graph shows distance (km) versus time (hours) for a car journey. The line starts at the origin and has slope 80. What does the slope represent?  The car travels at 80 km\/h.    "
